WEBVTT

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:11.760
Kitto saigo wa koko ni...
<i>Surely in the end...</i>

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:15.170
...kaettekuru to omou
<i>...we will return to this place.</i>

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:18.470
Sekai no hajimari wo...
<i>The memory of how you and I watched...</i>

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:22.180
futari de miteita...
<i>the beginning of the world...</i>

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.050
...kioku
<i>...together.</i>

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:32.350
Karappo no karada ni...
<i>Memory gradually pours...</i>

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:36.190
...furitsumotte yuku kioku
<i>...into my empty body.</i>

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:39.460
Watashi wo sukoshi zutsu...
<i>Building me ever so slowly...</i>

00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:43.200
...tsukutte mitashite
<i>...and filling my being.</i>

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:46.240
Sonnafuu ni hito wa...
<i>That is how a man...</i>

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:49.770
...hito no katachi ni naru no
<i>...takes the shape of a man...</i>

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:53.580
Wasuretakunai omoi...
<i>...as emotions he doesn't want to forget...</i>

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:57.210
...kokoro ni kasanete
<i>...rest in his heart.</i>

00:00:57.290 --> 00:01:00.720
Dokomade tooku yuku toki nimo...
<i>No matter how far away you</i> go...

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:04.160
...watashi wa koko ni kimi no naka ni
<i>...I am here inside of you.</i>

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:07.820
Kimi wo michibiku hoshi no youni...
<i>Like the star that guides you...</i>

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:11.230
...zutto iruwa
<i>...I will be here forever.</i>

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:14.860
Kimi wo hanareteiku toki nimo...
<i>Even when I am drifting from you...</i>

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:18.270
mune ni kizanda ano basho e to...
<i>I will probably be able to</i> go...

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:21.830
...watashi wa kitto kaereru kara
<i>...to the place burned into my memory.</i>

00:01:21.910 --> 00:01:27.870
Furimukazuni yukuwa
<i>So I will go, without turning back.</i>

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:48.800
Here you go! The
Edomae Tempura special dish!

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:52.300
Great! I've been waiting for that!

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:53.860
You got it!

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:57.680
The rest of the world
is celebrating Christmas.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:01.810
Isn't dinner on this
tiny cruiser a little low-key?

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:07.250
Don't be greedy. This is
all free. And we were invited.

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:10.260
This is good stuff. Right?

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:15.250
Aw... Well, if this cruise came
with a day-pass at Tokyo Disneyland...

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:19.460
...AND a boyfriend, and we didn't
have to think about tonight...

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:22.560
...then I wouldn't have any complaints.

00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:26.710
Yukichin, you should be more nervous.

00:02:26.770 --> 00:02:30.770
But If I get nervous now, I'll be a total wreck
by the time it comes to the showdown.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:36.070
I think I'm a little seasick...

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:45.990
Mai is too nervous.
Do you think we can do it?

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:53.020
We have two high school girls,
one middle-aged man, and...

00:02:55.670 --> 00:02:59.370
I guess that makes us
a second-rate Charlie's Angels.

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:07.540
We can't turn back now.

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:50.520
Right on schedule.
We'll carry it out tonight.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:03.530
He says tonight's the night.

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:05.440
Can't we postpone?

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:10.000
We're not the only ones
involved in this, you know.

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:15.510
I can do it. I'm okay.

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:18.410
- See ya!
- You got it!

00:04:31.030 --> 00:04:34.400
I looked into your story.

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:36.560
You didn't believe me?

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:38.540
Well, I like to make sure of things myself.

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:41.640
Some of the players' character data...

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:44.540
...their data volume is much larger
than the system specs.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:48.270
However, if you track them
for a period of time...

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:50.940
...the data volume reverts to their
normal size before you know it.

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:53.490
Does that mean the
data is being exchanged...

00:04:53.550 --> 00:04:56.490
...inside the system without permission?

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:00.120
Well, yes, that's what it would mean.

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:02.560
In other words, that is the
"outside" Harald brought in.

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:06.990
The "outside"...I still don't get what that is.

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:12.670
Harald was in love with Emma Wielant.
We assume that after her death...

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:16.070
...Harald may have tried to put
his love for her into a tangible form.

00:05:32.090 --> 00:05:34.760
It's not the end yet...

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:37.460
I won't let it end.

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:41.600
You're talking about "Fragment," right?

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:47.130
This is only a theory, but we believe
"Fragment" was merely a container.

00:05:47.210 --> 00:05:52.370
I do not want to give you the wrong
impression, but what he tried to leave...

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:55.080
...was a child between Emma and himself.

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:57.050
What?!

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:05.060
A girl...

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:10.690
Wait, wait. Don't you
think that's a little too... -

00:06:11.230 --> 00:06:16.530
I am, of course, only speaking figuratively.
The child in this case would be an Al.

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:17.870
Artificial Intelligence?

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:21.880
Yes. An Al capable of learning and making
mistakes like human beings.

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:23.640
The ultimate Al.

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:27.850
That tolerates "wavering"...

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:32.750
I get it. The inflated data was
the players' persona data.

00:06:32.820 --> 00:06:36.810
That's right. In the game,
characters, enemies, equipment...

00:06:36.890 --> 00:06:40.550
...and even the fields, are equal in data.

00:06:40.630 --> 00:06:43.620
The engine that Harald designed passes
various persona data to the system...

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:47.900
...via money or weapons
that is traded in the game.

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:50.730
The data is then reflected into
the growth of the ultimate Al.

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:53.230
That's what it originally was.

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:56.870
What was Harald's miscalculation?

00:06:56.940 --> 00:07:00.280
He probably didn't
know much about women.

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:02.250
Huh? What's that supposed to mean?

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:05.290
As the data exchange went on,
the system itself...

00:07:05.350 --> 00:07:08.250
...came to possess
an artificial persona as well.

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:10.620
An artificial maternal mind.

00:07:10.690 --> 00:07:16.130
In other words, she, the system,
exists only to give birth to the Al.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:20.630
Which means the moment
the Al is born, her duty will end.

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:26.100
So that's why the system is refusing
to give birth to the ultimate Al?

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:30.300
Yes. The system is using every method
conceivable to prevent that from taking place.

00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:35.940
I suspect that is the true cause
behind the incidents in "The World."

00:07:36.020 --> 00:07:39.250
That thing, that ultimate Al thing...

00:07:39.320 --> 00:07:41.120
...had better be something
that's worth all this trouble...

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:43.120
...or someone's got some explaining to do.

00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:47.250
All we can do is hope that whatever it is...

00:07:47.330 --> 00:07:49.590
...it's something wonderful.

00:08:17.360 --> 00:08:19.690
Hey, can I ask something basic?

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:21.360
Go ahead.

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:25.960
You can get to this place by land on roads,
right? Why did we bother coming by sea?

00:08:27.670 --> 00:08:30.300
Hey, weren't you paying attention?

00:08:30.370 --> 00:08:31.670
Huh?

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:34.670
The Maritime Information
Backup Center is active.

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:39.240
Though it may have no guards stationed,
there is a security system in place.

00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:54.220
Sure doesn't look like it.

00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:58.700
The seaside security is less tight
due to their financial situation.

00:08:58.770 --> 00:09:03.330
It'll buy us a little time... or so I heard.

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:08.240
Still, Helba is a super hacker, right?

00:09:08.310 --> 00:09:11.840
Why can't she do anything
about the security system?

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:15.720
Have you forgotten
about Network Crisis?

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:20.020
The malice of "The World"
isn't restricted to the net anymore.

00:09:20.090 --> 00:09:22.780
If we aren't careful,
we'll be spotted right away.

00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:27.390
I don't want it to know our moves
until the last possible moment.

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:28.930
Please understand.

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:32.630
Get moving!

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:56.450
My heart is pounding.

00:09:57.190 --> 00:09:59.090
I think I'm going to throw up.

00:09:59.830 --> 00:10:01.390
Are you still seasick?

00:10:01.460 --> 00:10:03.290
She's just nervous.

00:10:09.870 --> 00:10:12.070
You don't have to hold it back.

00:10:12.140 --> 00:10:13.610
I'm okay.

00:10:45.340 --> 00:10:48.100
The security company will definitely
come here to look at least once.

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:52.130
If we're lucky, they'll think it
was a false alarm. But if we aren't...

00:10:53.210 --> 00:10:54.840
I don't want to think about it.

00:10:56.150 --> 00:10:57.950
Get moving!

00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:00.990
Hey...!

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:20.840
How much time do you need to set it up?

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:22.840
- 20 minutes.
- 10 minutes.

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:24.500
That's impossible.

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:27.570
If you say 20 minutes, it will take 25.

00:11:27.650 --> 00:11:30.810
But if you say 10 minutes
and take 15, that's fine.

00:11:32.550 --> 00:11:35.950
Come again? I don't like him.

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:46.700
Hey... I'm here because I
want to learn about the "outside"...

00:11:46.770 --> 00:11:51.730
...that Harald brought into the
game, but why are you here?

00:11:52.610 --> 00:11:55.170
I want to know, too, y'know.

00:11:55.240 --> 00:11:57.540
- Want to know what?
- You know...

00:11:57.610 --> 00:12:01.100
Yukichin? Sorry. Could
you get me some coffee?

00:12:01.180 --> 00:12:01.880
What?

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:05.650
There's a vending machine
over there. I'll go with you.

00:12:05.720 --> 00:12:08.850
It's okay. I can go by myself.

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:10.480
Yeesh.

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:16.450
Why so snappy?
I thought you guys were friends.

00:12:17.230 --> 00:12:21.500
Didn't someone once say
that if you want to stay friends...

00:12:21.570 --> 00:12:24.130
...you shouldn't meet in person?

00:12:25.570 --> 00:12:29.630
I don't know about being friends with
someone you've never met before, though.

00:12:35.380 --> 00:12:37.480
Stupid Kyo.

00:12:50.400 --> 00:12:52.020
Would somebody get that?

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:56.970
Hello? I understand.

00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:01.910
It was Mr. Sato. He says a car
from the security company is coming.

00:13:07.250 --> 00:13:08.940
I'm back!

00:13:09.020 --> 00:13:10.640
Quiet!

00:13:20.030 --> 00:13:22.150
Come on, let's get this over with.

00:13:24.060 --> 00:13:25.500
All right. Let's get going.

00:13:51.060 --> 00:13:53.690
Nobody's gone in or out since this evening.

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:01.530
Want to go in and check?

00:14:20.490 --> 00:14:22.390
It's probably another false alarm.

00:14:22.460 --> 00:14:25.820
There's been a lot of
that since the Network Crisis.

00:14:33.430 --> 00:14:36.160
This is Megafloat Maritime
Information Backup Center...

00:14:36.240 --> 00:14:37.700
Wait, look!

00:14:37.770 --> 00:14:40.970
Someone used the vending
machine about 5 minutes ago!

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:54.920
Even with the hardware here,
there's too much data to handle.

00:14:56.220 --> 00:14:58.710
Oh, it's okay. Yeah, yeah?

00:14:58.790 --> 00:15:01.730
- We have a problem.
- Same here.

00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:04.320
- That's not good.
- That's all you've got to say?

00:15:04.400 --> 00:15:07.600
Putting that aside,
please send Kyo to me.

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:09.570
But what about here?

00:15:09.640 --> 00:15:11.540
Well, in any event...

00:15:11.610 --> 00:15:15.100
...that's a type of problem that
only you can handle, isn't it?

00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:18.570
I really don't like him...

00:15:42.800 --> 00:15:44.130
So they know we're here?

00:15:44.200 --> 00:15:47.070
To say the least, yes.

00:15:47.140 --> 00:15:49.440
So we may go into battle!

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:51.500
Get serious!

00:15:51.580 --> 00:15:53.640
Kyo...

00:15:53.710 --> 00:15:57.810
There are games you can't reset.
We'll have to withstand this somehow.

00:16:11.730 --> 00:16:14.830
Sorry. I yawn every time I get nervous.

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:19.400
My mom scolded me a lot for it.
She said I wasn't being serious.

00:16:20.140 --> 00:16:23.410
Your brain lacks oxygen.
Take deep breaths.

00:16:33.790 --> 00:16:34.810
How is it?

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:37.150
I can't tell.

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:41.180
I see. Even my magic
doesn't work on you.

00:16:42.860 --> 00:16:47.160
Well, could you start
monitoring the game?

00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:48.700
Sure.

00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:53.300
- This isn't funny.
- Tell me about it.

00:16:54.170 --> 00:17:01.550
Our goal is to buy time until
the server we set up can be operational.

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:03.110
Do you understand?

00:17:03.180 --> 00:17:04.650
Yes, sir!

00:17:05.820 --> 00:17:07.810
Well, meeting adjourned.

00:17:12.290 --> 00:17:13.820
You seem to be enjoying yourself.

00:17:13.890 --> 00:17:16.620
Who, me? Yeah!

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:18.670
Why? Why are you?

00:17:18.730 --> 00:17:21.200
Because the old me is dead.

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:27.230
Now, I'm having a great time doing stuff
with you, Mai and that funny Tokuoka guy.

00:17:27.640 --> 00:17:30.580
Yeah, but if we're caught, we're criminals.

00:17:30.640 --> 00:17:33.640
If that happens, then we'll
fight CC Corp. in court.

00:17:33.710 --> 00:17:35.840
- Huh?!
- Right?

00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:40.340
You're a scary girl.

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:47.350
If this doesn't work, I give up.

00:17:52.900 --> 00:17:54.560
It's working!

00:17:55.240 --> 00:17:57.170
How did you do it?

00:17:57.240 --> 00:18:00.070
Distributed processing.
Since I've got all of these machines...

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:03.130
...why not use them all?
How is your side?

00:18:03.210 --> 00:18:05.410
There doesn't seem to be
anything going on yet.

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:07.910
It looks like we'll make it in time.

00:18:11.720 --> 00:18:13.210
No problem back there!

00:18:13.290 --> 00:18:14.910
What's going on?!

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:19.960
That battle thing you said isn't funny.

00:18:21.060 --> 00:18:22.720
Hey!

00:18:27.630 --> 00:18:31.330
We're ready. All we have to do
now is link to Helba's server.

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:36.710
- Mr. Tokuoka...
- Yes?

00:18:36.780 --> 00:18:38.240
It's coming.

00:18:39.110 --> 00:18:40.740
...Got it.

00:18:42.280 --> 00:18:43.770
Please hurry!

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:49.320
You and I will go to the
Control Room. And you two...

00:18:55.330 --> 00:18:56.320
Hey!

00:19:06.640 --> 00:19:09.540
I hate this! This isn't
what I'm supposed to do!

00:19:09.610 --> 00:19:11.080
Stop complaining!

00:19:12.010 --> 00:19:13.640
Mr. Tokuoka, now!

00:19:18.690 --> 00:19:20.380
I don't believe this.

00:19:21.360 --> 00:19:23.380
I've spotted a suspicious
cruiser on the shore.

00:19:24.090 --> 00:19:25.890
Stay there and keep watch!

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:29.960
You guys return to the car!

00:19:30.030 --> 00:19:31.830
Are you sure?!

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:33.920
The two of us can handle it!

00:19:40.540 --> 00:19:41.010
Sickened

00:19:41.380 --> 00:19:41.840
Imprisoned

00:19:42.240 --> 00:19:42.710
Fallen Angel

00:19:43.080 --> 00:19:46.050
Message Reads: Balmung of the Azure Sky, Orca of the
Azure Sea, I do not want to lose to you!

00:19:46.710 --> 00:19:48.340
Tomonari?

00:19:54.390 --> 00:19:55.290
What happened?

00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:57.850
I don't know. I don't know, but suddenly...

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:17.530
Tomonari is fighting inside the game.

00:20:17.610 --> 00:20:19.080
Huh?!

00:20:28.490 --> 00:20:31.920
They must be planning to escape down
the fire escape... Nah, ignore them.

00:20:31.990 --> 00:20:33.050
But...

00:20:33.130 --> 00:20:36.100
They can't get out from the
Megafloat anyway. Get moving.

00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:48.410
Mr. Tokuoka, I can't hold on!
Everyone will disappear!

00:20:48.480 --> 00:20:52.040
The set up is accurate,
nothing wrong with the wiring.

00:20:52.110 --> 00:20:54.380
There's no reason it shouldn't connect!

00:20:54.450 --> 00:20:56.080
Help...

00:20:56.150 --> 00:20:57.620
Mai?!

00:21:07.460 --> 00:21:08.930
You!

00:21:10.130 --> 00:21:11.690
You know the consequences, right?!

00:21:13.170 --> 00:21:14.790
Are you all right?

00:21:17.470 --> 00:21:19.800
Unfortunately, we're out of time.

00:21:20.410 --> 00:21:22.400
- No.
- But...

00:21:22.480 --> 00:21:25.810
I saw everybody fighting for it.
Tomonari playing Sieg...

00:21:25.880 --> 00:21:27.440
...and someone named Orca.

00:21:27.510 --> 00:21:29.540
If we stop now, everybody will...

00:21:30.180 --> 00:21:31.810
We won't stop.

00:21:33.150 --> 00:21:35.050
There are no errors on this end...

00:21:35.120 --> 00:21:38.820
...which means there must be a problem
on the other side. If that's the case...

00:21:39.860 --> 00:21:41.450
You're kidding!

00:21:41.530 --> 00:21:42.460
What?

00:21:42.530 --> 00:21:44.390
Discard the other server.

00:21:44.460 --> 00:21:49.090
Then this server will pretend
as if it was the other server.

00:21:49.170 --> 00:21:51.500
But if we miss the timing...

00:21:52.440 --> 00:21:58.110
Everyone could become comatose,
but it's the only thing I can think of.

00:21:59.510 --> 00:22:01.140
Huh? That's strange.

00:22:08.090 --> 00:22:09.580
Let me do it.

00:22:10.190 --> 00:22:12.520
Wait. I'll contact the other side.

00:22:14.530 --> 00:22:16.020
I don't want any part of this!

00:22:16.100 --> 00:22:18.120
Move your feet, not your mouth!

00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:23.100
Let's do it. She says
she'll leave the timing to us.

00:22:25.910 --> 00:22:28.030
React faster than light.

00:23:39.680 --> 00:23:43.640
That's why I said this isn't
what I'm supposed to be doing.

00:23:44.550 --> 00:23:46.040
It's too late for that.

00:23:46.650 --> 00:23:48.750
You won't put up a fight, right?

00:23:50.620 --> 00:23:52.680
You can if you want, though.

00:23:57.330 --> 00:23:59.760
- I'm sorry!
- He'll live.

00:24:01.030 --> 00:24:03.000
C'mon! Mai, let's hurry!

00:24:06.310 --> 00:24:08.000
Why, you!

00:24:10.680 --> 00:24:12.140
What the hell?

00:24:12.580 --> 00:24:14.510
Pleased to meet you.

00:24:15.680 --> 00:24:17.980
This is my business card.

00:24:19.320 --> 00:24:21.910
Network security analyst?

00:24:21.990 --> 00:24:27.980
Yes. There seems to be number of problems
with this information backup center.

00:24:28.860 --> 00:24:31.920
We can go into details
back at the office.

00:24:32.000 --> 00:24:34.970
What the hell are you talking about?!

00:24:35.040 --> 00:24:36.500
Yes?

00:24:40.310 --> 00:24:41.640
- Run!
- But...

00:24:41.710 --> 00:24:43.340
I'll handle it, now go!

00:24:44.410 --> 00:24:46.280
Kyo! Get them to safety!

00:24:46.780 --> 00:24:48.750
But Mr. Tokuoka...

00:24:48.820 --> 00:24:51.810
Are you two going to
let his efforts go to waste?!

00:24:54.190 --> 00:24:56.280
C- Call for backup!

00:24:56.360 --> 00:25:00.290
Mai, let me have a chance
to shine for once, will you?

00:25:03.060 --> 00:25:04.530
Let's go!

00:25:09.800 --> 00:25:12.360
Intruders spotted in container
block! Call for backup!

00:25:15.740 --> 00:25:17.330
Why can't you just
leave things alone?!

00:25:17.410 --> 00:25:18.310
Damn you! Stop!!
But...

00:25:18.310 --> 00:25:19.800
Damn you! Stop!!
Shut up!

00:25:30.390 --> 00:25:32.380
- Take us out!
- You got it!

00:25:33.790 --> 00:25:35.760
You won't get away from me! Hey!

00:25:40.970 --> 00:25:42.800
You know that, right?

00:25:44.770 --> 00:25:46.240
Ow!

00:25:57.750 --> 00:25:59.240
Ow.

00:26:00.450 --> 00:26:03.720
I told you, I caught one of 'em!

00:26:03.790 --> 00:26:05.920
How should I know
how many there are?!

00:26:06.990 --> 00:26:10.660
All right, let's talk about that along with
the rest of the business, shall we?

00:26:11.100 --> 00:26:13.070
Hey! Hey!

00:26:20.140 --> 00:26:23.740
So you don't know
what happened after that?

00:26:23.810 --> 00:26:25.780
- Everything is okay.
- How do you know?

00:26:32.750 --> 00:26:35.410
Because that's the will of
the ultimate Al...

00:26:36.820 --> 00:26:39.790
...the will of the girl who's
trying to be born.

00:27:18.600 --> 00:27:20.570
Hey, it's snowing.

00:27:23.440 --> 00:27:24.800
It's Christmas.

00:27:24.870 --> 00:27:26.840
But Mr. Tokuoka is...

00:28:10.820 --> 00:28:14.180
Hey! How are you doing, comrades?

00:28:14.250 --> 00:28:17.490
How about you? I guess
we lost our evidence.

00:28:23.900 --> 00:28:25.690
Did not.

00:28:38.180 --> 00:28:41.940
Okay, let's get something
good to eat.

00:28:42.920 --> 00:28:45.040
- All right!
- Hear, hear!

00:29:00.030 --> 00:29:04.490
Tasogare no umi ni dete...
<i>Setting out in twilight seas...</i>

00:29:04.570 --> 00:29:09.480
Futari wa nidoto mou meguri...
<i>Will we never meet...</i>

00:29:09.480 --> 00:29:14.540
...aenaino?
<i>...again?</i>

00:29:21.250 --> 00:29:28.890
Kin no akari ga umi ni ochite...
<i>A light of gold falls into the sea...</i>

00:29:28.960 --> 00:29:34.260
...natsu no kaze ga togireta
<i>...the wind of summer trails off.</i>

00:29:34.330 --> 00:29:39.470
Obieru futari ni tada...
<i>The frightened pair only hears the sound...</i>

00:29:39.540 --> 00:29:45.640
...yosetekaesu mizuoto
<i>...of sea water coming and going again.</i>

00:29:47.310 --> 00:29:52.580
Donnani nami wo kasanete...
<i>No matter how I drown the waves...</i>

00:29:52.650 --> 00:29:57.920
Omoide wo sakendemo...
<i>Screaming out our memories...</i>

00:29:57.990 --> 00:30:03.220
Anata no ita kishibe niwa...
<i>I can never return to the shore...</i>

00:30:03.300 --> 00:30:09.030
...mou kaerenai
<i>...where you were.</i>

00:30:09.370 --> 00:30:13.930
Tasogare dake wo daite
<i>Embrace nothing but the twilight sky.</i>

00:30:14.010 --> 00:30:17.140
Ano hi no nami wa mou...
<i>The waves from that day are now...</i>

00:30:17.140 --> 00:30:20.910
...fukai umi no soko
<i>...at the bottom of the deep ocean.</i>

00:30:20.980 --> 00:30:24.540
Kanashimi wo shiranai...
<i>They sleep as they embrace blue dreams...</i>

00:30:24.620 --> 00:30:29.750
...aoi yume wo mite nemutteiru
<i>...that do not know sorrow.</i>
